# DOM Element IDs

Use **namespaced kebab-case** `id` attributes on **considerable** elements so developers can find them quickly in DevTools (`#users-page-search-input`).

Primary use: **developer debugging** — not E2E `data-testid` (out of scope unless added separately).

Layout ids **complement** control ids (inputs, buttons) — apply both where relevant.

## Helpers

```tsx
import {
  APP_LAYOUT_ID,
  buildDomId,
  dialogSectionIds,
  panelSectionIds,
} from "@/shared/utils/domId";
```

Implementation: [`front-end/src/shared/utils/domId.ts`](front-end/src/shared/utils/domId.ts).

## Naming

**Format:** `{domain}-{surface}-{element}` — minimum **2 segments**, never bare `name` or `email`.

| Segment | Examples |
|---------|----------|
| domain | `users`, `tags`, `company-settings`, `auth-login`, `app` |
| surface | `page`, `create-dialog`, `filters`, `registration-step-location` |
| element | `page-header`, `search-input`, `add-button`, `name-input` |

**Control suffixes:** `-input`, `-textarea`, `-submit-button`, `-cancel-button`.

**Layout suffixes:** see table below.

**Dynamic lists:** append entity id — `users-list-row-{userId}`.

**Labels:** `htmlFor` on `Label` must match the control `id` exactly.

## Layout div regions

| Layer | Element suffix | Example |
|-------|----------------|---------|
| App | `layout-root`, `layout-body`, `layout-header`, `layout-sidebar`, `layout-sidebar-nav`, `layout-main-content`, `layout-mobile-overlay` | `app-layout-main-content` |
| Page | `page`, `page-inner`, `page-header`, `page-header-actions`, `page-stats`, `page-filters`, `page-body`, `page-body-inner`, `page-skeleton`, `page-list`, `page-pagination`, `page-empty-state` | `spaces-page-body` |
| Dialog | `{surface}-dialog`, `{surface}-dialog-header`, `{surface}-dialog-body`, `{surface}-dialog-footer` | `tags-form-dialog-body` |
| Panel | `{surface}-panel`, `{surface}-panel-header`, `{surface}-panel-body` | `users-page-filters-panel-body` |

### App shell (singleton)

Use `APP_LAYOUT_ID` in [`MainLayout.tsx`](front-end/src/layouts/MainLayout.tsx), [`Header.tsx`](front-end/src/layouts/Header.tsx), [`Sidebar.tsx`](front-end/src/layouts/Sidebar.tsx).

### Page list shell

Per-file `ID` const — see [list-page-shell.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-page-shell.mdc) and [`UsersPage.tsx`](front-end/src/features/users/pages/UsersPage/UsersPage.tsx).

### Dialog sections

Pass `id` to [`CustomDialog`](front-end/src/components/ui/custom-dialog.tsx); header/body/footer ids are derived as `{id}-header`, `{id}-body`, `{id}-footer`.

### Filter panels

Pass `id` to [`RightPanel`](front-end/src/components/common/RightPanel.tsx); header/body ids derived as `{id}-header`, `{id}-body`.

## What gets an id

1. **Layout regions** — app shell, page root/sections, dialog/panel sections (above)
2. Dialog/sheet root, form root, footer primary/cancel actions
3. Form fields (inputs, textareas, selects, checkboxes with labels)
4. Primary header actions (Add/Create/Save)
5. Search, filter toggle, view switcher

**Skip:** decorative wrappers, icons, individual skeleton cells, every inner card div.

## Anti-patterns

- Generic single-word ids: `name`, `email`, `address`, `active`
- Duplicate ids on the same rendered document
- Replacing shadcn `FormItem` `useId()` — keep opaque ids for a11y wiring; use explicit `buildDomId` for raw `Label`/`Input` dialogs ([form-dialogs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/form-dialogs.mdc))

